{"summary":"System: Regional Dispatch Center (alias/call sign: Juniper) provides 24/7 intake, triage support, ambulance dispatch, regional coordination, and shared operational picture for emergency medical requests. Mandate: translate reported emergencies into prioritized incidents and coordinate appropriate response under approved clinical/jurisdictional protocols. Participating jurisdictions retain resource ownership/local policy responsibility; regional service coordinates agreed response activity.

Actors/elements: Call Taker Mara obtains incident details/location and enters request for assessment via Computer Aided Dispatch Console (CAD Console). Triage Supervisor reviews incident information, assigns/confirms priority, directs clinical review. Regional Medical Director owns clinical triage policy/limits. Dispatch personnel apply protocols, seek clinical guidance beyond delegated authority, select routes/ETAs considering travel time, road restrictions, weather, closures, distance, road access, and available ambulance capacity. Shift Commander (Sundial) is on-duty operational authority for coordination/service continuity, surge priorities, conflict resolution, jurisdictional escalation; must not replace Medical Director clinical-policy authority or Paramedic Crew scene judgment. Radio Coordinator (Mistral) manages/monitors Regional Radio Network, maintains communications discipline among dispatch/ambulance crews, confirms assigned channels/backups at shift start; radio checks verify weak-signal coverage and equipment/network problems. Fleet Maintenance Cell (Bluejay) provides operational awareness of vehicle serviceability/maintenance constraints; monitors vehicle availability, scheduled servicing, defects reducing zone coverage. Data Quality Officer reviews dispatch records for completeness, consistency, and information-handling compliance. Paramedic Crew provides immediate patient assessment/care. Ambulance Unit 417 is in regional response pool when assigned. Hospital Liaison Desk coordinates receiving capacity/destination constraints. Emergency Department sends receiving considerations. Riverside Trauma Center is designated destination.

Items/flows: reported emergency -> Call Taker Mara -> CAD Console/request for assessment; incident information -> Triage Supervisor; priority/clinical-review direction -> dispatch. Regional Radio Network carries dispatch/coordination communications. Ambulance Coordination Platform maintains incidents, unit assignments, resource status. Fleet Maintenance Cell produces Battery Swap Voucher documenting authorized battery replacement. Defined response zones have boundaries maintained with jurisdictions and reviewed when roads/population/service agreements change; each zone has primary/alternate routes to Emergency Department and Riverside Trauma Center subject to clinical direction/access conditions. Crews verify rapidly changing access before constrained routes. North Gate Status Board provides northern access/queue and produces North Approach Queue Snapshot. South Gate Status Board provides southern access/restrictions. Both gate boards checked at shift start and access changes. Readiness checks confirm staffing, communications, clinical supplies, fuel, vehicle condition, maintenance restrictions."}
